## Interlude / Side B — English Translation (Chapters 40–44 + 5 Ending Closings)
## Source: game/story/bab_40_44.rpy

################################################################################
## CHAPTER 40 — A Parcel at the Edge of Time
################################################################################

translate en b40_001:
    "August first. It's finally here, no putting it off. Malang's sky feels strange this morning — not overcast, not bright. Cool, quiet. Like the whole city is holding its breath, waiting for late afternoon."

translate en b40_002:
    kai_hati "Today. Today's the day that train leaves. Today, those words on the red tape… actually happen."

translate en b40_003:
    "Kai opens the front door just to get some air. His eyes stop right on the woven doormat. There's a small package wrapped in brown paper. No sender's name. Just black-ink handwriting he knows by heart: \"For Kai.\""

translate en b40_004:
    kai_hati "Yara's handwriting. {i}(swallows hard){/i} …How long has this been sitting here?"

translate en b40_005:
    "Back in his room, Kai tears the wrapping open slowly, like he's afraid of ripping whatever's inside. Inside is a clear plastic cassette. Not a red tape. Just a regular Type II Chrome — the kind Yara always uses for her everyday recordings. Tucked inside is a tiny note: \"Play me.\""

translate en b40_006:
    kai "{i}(picks up his dusty silver Walkman){/i} …Okay. Okay, Yar."

translate en b40_007:
    "Laughter. A whole compilation of the two of them laughing. Yara cracking up when they nearly slipped into the mud by the rice fields near Bukit Banyak. Kai's own laugh — carefree, unfamiliar, like someone else's voice — when they finally caught the blare of an old train horn. The rush of night wind. Rain pattering on the porch of Pak Ageng's shop. Rustling branches."

translate en b40_008a:
    "Between the laughs, the sound of a boiling pot in the cafeteria rises right to the front, crystal clear — the very first sound Kai ever recorded for Yara."

translate en b40_008b:
    "Between the laughs, the sound of rain hitting the gutter rises right to the front, steady and patient — the recording Kai picked out on the shop porch."

translate en b40_008c:
    "Between the laughs, the hiss of blank tape rises right to the front for two seconds — the sound of \"silence\" Kai used to dread most, now nothing more than a pause between laughs."

translate en b40_009:
    kai_hati "That's… that's us. That's really us. We sound… so alive. So close. {i}(tears roll down his cheeks){/i} Even though my memory of the library is still a blank hole. Still empty. This — my chest remembers. My chest remembers all of it."

translate en b40_010:
    "The tape keeps rolling. The city noise on the recording fades out. Clean. Then Yara's voice comes in — not the cold Yara from school lately. The gentle Yara. A little hoarse from holding back emotion."

translate en b40_011:
    yara_kaset "Kai… I don't know what actually happened to you. I don't know why you suddenly pulled away. Why the way you looked at me turned so stiff. Why you chose to lock yourself up in silence."

translate en b40_012:
    yara_kaset "{i}(a sharp breath brushes the mic){/i} But I want you to know… out of all the noise in this world that I can't stand, the sound of you laughing while we went sound-hunting is the prettiest melody I've ever recorded. I'm glad I got to know you, Kai. I'm… really glad."

translate en b40_013:
    kai "{i}(yanks off the earphones, staring at the wall clock — 10:00 AM){/i} …This afternoon. Her train's this afternoon. {i}(clenches his fists){/i} Like Pak Ageng said yesterday… a tape records sound, not feelings. Who decides whether those tears are out of regret or out of missing someone… that's me. Only me."

translate en b40_014:
    kai_hati "Six months of running from today. Six whole months. {i}(stands up){/i} That's enough. I'm not losing her without doing anything. Not anymore."

translate en b40_015:
    "Kai opens his desk drawer. There's a blank tape he's never used — he wants Yara to take something of his with her too, not just the other way around. His hand pauses. There are a few things he could slip in with it."

translate en b40_016a:
    kai_hati "The little blank tape from Pak Ageng. He told me back then: who knows, maybe one day you'll need to record something that's truly yours. {i}(smiles faintly){/i} Turns out it's not for me. It's for her. So once she's in Jogja, she can send her voice back."

translate en b40_016b:
    kai_hati "I rewrote it four times. The first one was way too long. The second sounded like a formal letter. The third… was so honest it actually embarrassed me. The fourth is short. \"Listen to the tape once you get there. Not on the train. — K.\" …Yeah. That's all it needs."

translate en b40_016c:
    kai_hati "No. No extras. If I have something to say, I'll say it to her face. Out loud. With my own voice. That's… that's the whole point, isn't it?"

translate en b40_017:
    "The little parcel goes into Kai's bag. Outside, the sky that's been holding back since morning starts to shift color."


################################################################################
## CHAPTER 41 — Cutting the Tape of Fate
################################################################################

translate en b41_001:
    kai "{i}(stares at the clock — 2:00 PM){/i} …Idiot. God, I'm such an idiot."

translate en b41_002:
    "The realization hits like a wave slamming into rock. For the past six months, Kai's been a slave to his own fear."

translate en b41_002_p2:
    "He locked himself inside a cage of predictions, letting his present rot away just because he was terrified of the end of a song he didn't even understand. That red tape never sealed his fate. It only recorded his despair — which came true because he gave up first."

translate en b41_003:
    kai "The tape wasn't to blame. {i}(grabs his gray jacket off the chair){/i} I'm the one who kept believing it. I'm the one who kept staying quiet. {i}(pauses){/i} Wes. That's enough."

translate en b41_004:
    kai_hati "I don't care about the tangled tape on that desk anymore. I don't care about the holes in my memory. Only one thing matters right now: Yara. Her train leaves this afternoon."

translate en b41_005:
    "Kai snatches his motorbike keys by the door, pushes the front door open — and the Malang sky that's been holding back all day finally breaks. Pouring rain, heavy wind, every mango tree along the neighborhood swaying hard."

translate en b41_006:
    kai "{i}(hops on the bike, kick-starting the engine in one stomp){/i} Rain again. {i}(twists the throttle){/i} Fine. Might as well get soaked!"

translate en b41_007:
    "The bike shoots forward. Jalan Sukarno-Hatta is slick and flooded with puddles. Rain lashes his helmet visor until Kai has to flip it up — cold drops stinging his face and eyes. He weaves between crawling cars, splashing straight through intersections, ignoring angry horns blaring from every direction."

translate en b41_008:
    kai_hati "Gotta make it. Gotta make it before the sepur leaves. {i}(teeth chattering in the rain){/i} I'm not letting the crying on that tape turn into some meaningless goodbye. No way."

translate en b41_009:
    "Under rain pouring harder by the second, he has only one destination: Stasiun Malang Kota Lama. No magnetic tape is deciding this afternoon. His own feet are. His own voice is."


################################################################################
## CHAPTER 42 — Meeting at the Platform Edge
################################################################################

translate en b42_001:
    "Kai kills the engine in the parking lot, bike leaning crooked, no time to straighten it properly. He sprints through the blowing rain into the concourse packed with people taking shelter and travelers hauling cardboard boxes, backpacks, and dripping umbrellas. He's gasping for air. His gray jacket is drenched — water dripping off his hair and hem onto the station tiles."

translate en b42_002:
    kai_hati "Where… where is she… {i}(scans the crowd){/i} Wall clock — three fifteen. The train hasn't left yet. Not yet. Please, not yet."

translate en b42_003:
    "Near the ticket checkpoint, he spots her. Yara. Walking slowly, dragging a big black suitcase that looks way too heavy for her. The canvas bag with her tripod and recorder is still over her left shoulder. Her big black headphones aren't on her ears — just hanging limp around her neck."

translate en b42_004:
    kai "{i}(shouts, voice hoarse){/i} YARA!"

translate en b42_005:
    "The shout cuts straight through the station PA noise. Yara freezes. Her shoulders tense. Slowly she turns around — and her puffy eyes go wide at the sight of Kai: soaked head to toe, chest heaving, standing in the middle of the crowd."

translate en b42_006:
    yara "{i}(barely audible){/i} Kai…? Why are you… why are you completely drenched like this?"

translate en b42_007:
    "Just a few meters between them. Right here, every choice Kai has made since his first day at that shop — every tape, every silence, every time he ran — hangs in the balance."


################################################################################
## ENDING — HAPPY-TRUE (H1)
################################################################################

translate en b42_h1_001:
    "Yara stays frozen, her grip on the suitcase handle going slack. And Kai — for the first time in six months — doesn't back away."

translate en b42_h1_002a:
    "Stepping closer, Kai lifts up the little parcel. Inside, the mini blank tape from Pak Ageng rattles softly with every step."

translate en b42_h1_002b:
    "Stepping closer, Kai lifts up the little parcel. Inside is the short note he rewrote four times."

translate en b42_h1_002c:
    "Stepping closer, Kai's hands hold nothing besides that blank tape. Nothing in between. Just him and his own voice."

translate en b42_h1_003:
    kai "{i}(steps forward, still out of breath){/i} Yar… wait. Don't board yet. I… I have to say something. Right now. Right here."


################################################################################
## ENDING — HAPPY-HEALTHY (H2)
################################################################################

translate en b42_h2_001:
    "Yara looks at Kai, dripping wet, and then — catching even Kai off guard — she lets out a small laugh. A tired laugh, full of relief."

translate en b42_h2_002:
    yara "Seriously, you… {i}(shakes her head){/i} I waited at school all morning and you never showed up. And then you show up at the station looking like a cat that fell in a ditch."

translate en b42_h2_003:
    kai "{i}(still panting, letting out a short laugh too){/i} I… I swung by Pak Ageng's shop first. Wanted to drop off a quick hello. And then… yeah, the rain— whatever. Doesn't matter. {i}(catches his breath){/i} I just wanted to make sure I said this to your face. Not on a tape. Not in a note. Face to face."

translate en b42_h2_004:
    yara "Say what?"

translate en b42_h2_005:
    kai "Have a safe trip. {i}(pauses; his voice softens){/i} And thank you. For all the sounds you taught me to hear. I used to think this world was way too noisy, Yar. Turns out I just didn't know how to listen."

translate en b42_h2_006:
    "Kai pulls a small parcel out of his bag — a blank tape they filled together with recordings of their own voices before today. No predictions. No spoilers for tomorrow. Just their voices, recorded on purpose, to replay whenever either of them misses the other."

translate en b42_h2_007:
    yara "{i}(takes the parcel, smiling){/i} This one's just us, right? Not \"tomorrow.\" Not \"next year.\""

translate en b42_h2_008:
    kai "Just us. Today. As we are."

translate en b42_h2_009:
    yara "{i}(gives Kai a quick hug — brief, a little awkward against his wet jacket — then steps back with a small laugh){/i} You are soaking wet, seriously. {i}(wipes her eyes){/i} Take good care of yourself, okay, Kai?"

translate en b42_h2_010:
    kai "You too. In Jogja… record lots of stuff. Send it to me."

translate en b42_h2_011:
    yara "Count on it. {i}(lifts her suitcase handle, stepping backward toward the platform gate, eyes still on him){/i} Goodbye."

translate en b42_h2_012:
    "Those words are finally spoken. Yet on this path, they feel light. No tape coming to collect, no prophecy looming over them. Just two people parting ways because that's how life goes — promising, in their own voices, that this song isn't over yet."


################################################################################
## ENDING — OPEN / UNRESOLVED (G)
################################################################################

translate en b42_g_001:
    "Kai reaches the platform at the exact moment the train doors shut. The exact moment the conductor's whistle blows. Right on time — and still too late."

translate en b42_g_002:
    kai "{i}(runs alongside the moving train, waving frantically at the air){/i} Yara! YARA!"

translate en b42_g_003:
    "Behind a fogged-up window, a face turns. Yara. Her eyes go wide. She presses her palm against the glass. The train picks up speed — Kai runs, then half-runs, until all he can manage is a breathless brisk walk."

translate en b42_g_004:
    yara "{i}(from behind the window, her shout muffled by glass and the roar of wheels){/i} KAI?! What are— what are you doing—"

translate en b42_g_005:
    kai "{i}(shouting between gasps){/i} I… I wanted to tell you… all this time I… I—"

translate en b42_g_006:
    "Sixty seconds. That's about all the time they get — Kai running down the platform, Yara pressed to the window, both of them shouting without really hearing each other. The exact same sixty seconds as that first tape that started all of this."

translate en b42_g_007:
    yara "{i}(barely audible, one last time before distance wins){/i} Kai… I can't answer you right now."

translate en b42_g_008:
    "The train shoots out of the station, carrying her words away before they can become anything. Kai stands at the end of the platform, drenched and alone, staring down the empty tracks. No breakup. No promise. Nothing resolved."

translate en b42_g_009:
    "That night, in his room, the blank tape Pak Ageng gave him sits in Kai's hand. His finger hovers over the play button. If he presses it, maybe there's an answer. If he presses it, maybe there's nothing at all. His finger freezes. Trembling — then, with one long breath, he presses it."

translate en b42_g_009b:
    "There is no voice of Yara on the tape. No promised future recording. All that emerges from behind the tape hiss is one quiet, fragile old voice — a final farewell from a shopkeeper."

translate en b42_g_010:
    "— End of Side B."


################################################################################
## ENDING — SAD-IRONIC (S2)
################################################################################

translate en b42_s2_001:
    kai "{i}(steps forward fast, words spilling out uncontrollably){/i} Yar, listen to me first. I can explain. I pulled away because of the tape, Yar. That red tape. It showed me you were going to leave — you were crying, saying goodbye — I heard all of it before it even happened, I— I couldn't take it, so I—"

translate en b42_s2_002:
    yara "{i}(cuts him off, quiet){/i} …A tape?"

translate en b42_s2_003:
    kai "I traded away memories to hear the future. Our memories. The first time we met in the library — I don't even remember it anymore, Yar, it's just a blank hole — but it was for— I just wanted to be ready, I was just terrified of losing—"

translate en b42_s2_004:
    "Yara doesn't answer right away. She stares at Kai for a long time — not angry. Just the look of someone who's just realized something heartbreaking."

translate en b42_s2_005:
    yara "So this whole time… {i}(her voice drops low){/i} while you went quiet, while you pushed me away, while I kept thinking I did something wrong — you were off listening to a tape. About me. Without me."

translate en b42_s2_006:
    kai "Th-that's not what I meant—"

translate en b42_s2_007:
    yara "You traded away your memory of me… just to peek at how my story ends. {i}(shakes her head slowly; eyes glistening, voice flat){/i} Kai. You didn't come here for me."

translate en b42_s2_008:
    kai "Yar—"

translate en b42_s2_009:
    yara "You came here for that tape. To calm your own fears down. {i}(pulls up her suitcase handle; takes a step back){/i} I'm a person, Kai. Not… not some recording you can keep replaying until you feel better."

translate en b42_s2_010:
    "The boarding announcement chimes. Yara turns and walks toward the platform gate — not running, not rushing. Just walking. Like someone who's already done. Kai stands frozen in the middle of the concourse, the small parcel still in his hand, never given."

translate en b42_s2_011:
    kai_hati "That's not true… I came here for her. I ran through the rain for her. {i}(long pause){/i} …Right? It was for her, right? Not for… {i}(he can't even finish his own thought){/i}"

translate en b42_s2_012:
    "And Yara's crying that afternoon — caught for a moment as she climbed the train steps — sounded just like the red tape. Tears of regret. Exactly what Kai had been terrified of all along. The prediction came true this afternoon. And the one who made it come true: Kai himself."

translate en b42_s2_013:
    "Back home, at midnight, Kai finally plays the blank tape Pak Ageng gave him. The tape that was supposed to record potential happiness."

translate en b42_s2_014:
    "Silence. Sixty seconds on the dot. Then a click. Potential happiness that never amounted to anything."


################################################################################
## ENDING — SAD-PASSIVE (S1)
################################################################################

translate en b42_s1_001:
    "Three in the afternoon. In a room with the lights off, Kai sits on the floor, his back pressed against the foot of the bed. The little parcel for Yara sits on the desk — neat, dry, never taken anywhere. Next to it, the red tape. Next to that, a phone whose screen has been dark since yesterday."

translate en b42_s1_002:
    kai_hati "It's three now. Her train's… almost leaving. If I run right now — if I get on my bike right now — maybe I could still… {i}(a very long pause){/i} …Maybe. {i}(he doesn't stand up){/i}"

translate en b42_s1_003:
    "Three ten. Three twenty. Outside, the rain falls softly, politely — nothing like those other paths where someone has to run straight through it. In this room, the rain is just background noise."

translate en b42_s1_004:
    kai_hati "She must think I don't care. {i}(closes his eyes){/i} Fine. Let her think that. It's… easier that way. For her. For me too. {i}(his voice cracks){/i} …Liar. It's not easy. Not easy at all."

translate en b42_s1_005:
    "That afternoon slips right by. That night, Kai plays the red tape. Static. Crying. \"Goodbye.\" He plays it again. Static. Crying. \"Goodbye.\" Again."

translate en b42_s1_005_p2:
    "Until one night — who knows how many nights later — his Walkman lets out a harsh crunch. The tape tangles. Snarls up. Ruined for good. And Kai just stares at it, unsurprised, like someone who's been waiting for it to happen."

translate en b42_s1_006:
    "Years later. The alley is still there, though the shop at the end isn't a cassette shop anymore. The \"Gema Masa\" sign has come down. Now it's a busy coffee shop — warm lights, soft music, young people laughing at tables where cassette racks used to stand."

translate en b42_s1_007:
    "Kai stands across the alley. Older now. A messenger bag slung over his shoulder. He stares at the shop for a long time. His hand lifts halfway — like he's about to wave at someone inside who isn't even there. Then it drops back down."

translate en b42_s1_008:
    kai_hati "In there, there used to be… a rocking chair. Jasmine tea. An old man who… {i}(pauses){/i} I never even said goodbye to Pak Ageng. Never went back. After that day… never once."

translate en b42_s1_009:
    "A young barista steps out to toss the trash, glancing briefly at Kai — just some stranger standing across the alley for too long. Kai gives a small, awkward nod. Then he turns around. And walks home. He doesn't go in. He never goes in."


################################################################################
## CHAPTER 43 — Distance Turned Into Sound
################################################################################

translate en b43_001:
    "Kai steps forward. Small puddles form on the clean tiles from his dripping jacket. Those few meters vanish. Now he can see her up close: the tip of Yara's nose is red, dried tear tracks still on her cheeks."

translate en b43_002:
    kai "{i}(voice trembling, competing with the PA system){/i} I was scared, Yara."

translate en b43_003:
    kai "I was scared because of that tape. I heard you crying. I heard you saying goodbye. And I— I was a coward. I thought if I pulled away first, saying goodbye today wouldn't wreck us. {i}(his breath hitches){/i} I was terrified of losing my world… when it had only just started making sound again because you were in it."

translate en b43_004:
    "Yara stares at him. The words are messy. Completely bare. No more wall of ice torturing the two of them for months. A strange hush hangs between them for a beat amidst the station noise."

translate en b43_005:
    "Then Yara's shoulders start shaking. What comes out isn't anger — it's a small, bitter laugh that slowly melts into sobs. She's laughing and crying at the same time, covering her face with one hand while the other still grips her suitcase handle tight."

translate en b43_006:
    yara "{i}(between tears and laughter){/i} You… you really are the biggest idiot I've ever met, Kai."

translate en b43_007:
    kai "…I know."

translate en b43_008:
    yara "{i}(looks up; eyes wet, but warm again){/i} I'm going off to college, Kai. Not dying. We're just in different cities. Not different worlds!"

translate en b43_009:
    kai "{i}(falls silent){/i} …"

translate en b43_010:
    yara "{i}(takes a step closer; water drips off Kai's jacket onto her shoes, and she couldn't care less){/i} That \"goodbye\" you heard on the red tape — well yeah, because I literally have to get on this train this afternoon!"

translate en b43_010_p2:
    yara "Of course I'm crying, I'm leaving Malang, leaving home… leaving some clueless guy who ran to the station to see me off looking like a drowned stray cat!"

translate en b43_011:
    kai "{i}(lets out a short laugh, eyes tearing up too){/i} …Drowned stray cat. Yeah. Yeah, fair enough."

translate en b43_012:
    yara "{i}(wipes her tears roughly with the sleeve of her denim jacket){/i} Jogja's only a few hours away on this train, Kai. This train runs every single day. The sound of the tracks — we can listen to it together over the phone every night if you want. Why on earth did you have to complicate something so simple?"

translate en b43_013:
    "Kai looks past the platform gate at the tracks, then back at Yara. For the first time, \"distance\" doesn't sound like a sentence. It sounds like… a schedule. Something they can work around."

translate en b43_014:
    kai "Then… let's actually plan it. None of that \"later, later\" stuff. \"Later\" is dangerous for me, Yar. You know how I get."

translate en b43_015:
    yara "{i}(smiles faintly){/i} Hmm. Okay. How do you want to do this, Mr. Planner?"

translate en b43_016a:
    kai "Every Friday. Four in the afternoon. That's… around the time I first heard your voice in the library. Every Friday at four, we call. You tell me about Jogja, I'll tell you about Malang. Out loud. Not over text."

translate en b43_017a:
    yara "{i}(pauses a beat, then her smile widens){/i} …You remembered the time. Okay. Fridays at four. Don't you dare be late."

translate en b43_016b:
    kai "Forget schedules. Whenever you miss me, call. Whenever I miss you, I'll call. Doesn't matter what time. Even if you're recording, pick up first and say \"hold on\" or something."

translate en b43_017b:
    yara "{i}(laughs){/i} That's not even a rule, Kai, that's just… whatever. Honestly, that's so us. Okay. Whenever."

translate en b43_016c:
    kai "Let's… trade tapes. I mean — voice recordings. Every week I'll mail a tape to Jogja: my voice, the shop, sounds of Malang. You send yours back. Like letters, except with sound."

translate en b43_017c:
    yara "{i}(her eyes light up){/i} …Voice letters. {i}(nods quickly){/i} That. That's amazing. That is peak us. Okay, deal."

translate en b43_018:
    yara "Deal, then. {i}(holds up her pinky for a second, then lowers it with a small laugh){/i} Wes, stop crying already. You're gonna make me— {i}(her own voice breaks first){/i} …see what you did?"


################################################################################
## CHAPTER 44 — A Pause, Not an End
################################################################################

translate en b44_001:
    pengumuman "Attention passengers of the Malioboro Ekspres bound for Yogyakarta, your train is now ready at platform one. Please prepare your tickets and ID for boarding…"

translate en b44_002:
    "Their time is up. Yara looks straight at Kai. Every doubt, every bit of anger, and months of icy silence just evaporate — leaving only one crystal-clear truth: this second belongs to them."

translate en b44_003:
    "Yara lets go of her suitcase handle. Not caring that Kai's jacket is still soaking wet and freezing, she steps forward and wraps both arms tight around his neck. Hugging him with everything she's got — like she can swallow all the miles about to stretch between them right into that embrace."

translate en b44_004:
    "Kai freezes for a second. Yara's warmth seeps right through his cold jacket, spreading into a chest that's felt hollow for far too long. Slowly, he raises both arms and hugs her back — just as tight. His face buries into the crook of her neck. The scent of light rain and faint soap. The scent he's missed for months."

translate en b44_005:
    kai_hati "This is it. This is what that tape made me dread for months. {i}(pauses){/i} …So this is what it feels like. It's not scary. Sad, yeah. But not scary."

translate en b44_006:
    "Yara lets go slowly. Takes a step back. Looks up at Kai's face — wet now too, and not just from the rain. She draws a deep breath. Heavy. Shaky. Broken. The exact frequency recorded on that red tape."

translate en b44_007:
    yara "{i}(smiles through her tears; the tip of her nose red){/i} Take good care of yourself, okay, Kai?"

translate en b44_008:
    "Her voice shakes hard and breaks at the very end. Exactly how Kai heard it alone in his quiet room, months ago."

translate en b44_009:
    yara "{i}(grabs her suitcase handle, stepping backward toward the platform gate, never taking her eyes off Kai){/i} Goodbye."

translate en b44_010:
    "The word slips out. Real. Out in the open station air. And this time — Kai doesn't go weak. Doesn't shatter. There's no terror pounding in his chest."

translate en b44_011a:
    kai "{i}(smiles, tears falling, voice steady){/i} Goodbye, Yar. {i}(pauses){/i} See you Friday."

translate en b44_011b0:
    kai "{i}(smiles, tears falling, voice steady){/i} Goodbye, Yar. {i}(pauses){/i}"

translate en b44_011b:
    kai "…Call me when you get there. No matter how late."

translate en b44_011c0:
    kai "{i}(smiles, tears falling, voice steady){/i} Goodbye, Yar. {i}(pauses){/i}"

translate en b44_011c:
    kai "…I'm sending my first tape this week. Watch out for it."

translate en b44_012:
    "In his head, Pak Ageng's words finally click into place: a tape records sound, not feelings. \"Goodbye\" isn't a period. It's a comma. A sweet little comma — a promise that their song is still going, just moving onto a fresh tape."

translate en b44_013a:
    "Friday. At 3:59 in the afternoon, Kai's already sitting at his desk, phone in front of him like he's waiting for an exam to start. Four o'clock sharp — the screen lights up."

translate en b44_014a:
    yara_telepon "Hello? Testing, testing. Can you hear me, Malang?"

translate en b44_015a:
    kai "{i}(grins wide){/i} Loud and clear. Jogja too. Extra loud, actually."

translate en b44_016a:
    yara_telepon "Good. Guess that's all the distance there is. Not that far after all, right?"

translate en b44_013b:
    "Kai's phone rings at eleven at night while he's helping Pak Ageng straighten up the shelves. The screen reads: \"Yara — Jogja.\""

translate en b44_014b:
    kai "{i}(answers, whispering){/i} Hello? Why are you still up?"

translate en b44_015b:
    yara_telepon "Can't sleep. The crickets here sound different, Kai. Different from Malang. Here, listen. {i}(two seconds of silence, then crickets chirping through the line){/i} …Hear that?"

translate en b44_016b:
    kai "{i}(chuckles softly){/i} I hear it. Record that. Send it on a tape too."

translate en b44_013c:
    "A package from Jogja shows up a week later. One cassette, labeled in Yara's handwriting: \"Side A — Jogja, week one. Play when things feel quiet.\""

translate en b44_014c:
    yara_kaset "Hey, Kai. It's me, coming to you from a city whose train tracks sound just like the ones in Malang. Turns out they sound the same everywhere… {i}(soft laugh){/i} Listen to the rest yourself. Oh, and — it's your turn. I'm waiting for Side B."

translate en b44_015c:
    "Kai looks at the blank tape on his desk. This time, he knows exactly what to put on it."

translate en b44_017:
    "Distance, it turns out, can turn into sound. And sound — if both people want it to — never really goes away."
